WEBVTT

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:10.940
Subaru...

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:11.780
Subaru...

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.490
Subarun...

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.370
Everyone...

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.500
Are you all right?

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.500
Are you hurt anywhere?

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.500
Welcome back.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.000
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.040
Thank you, Subaru.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.630
All of the fragments have returned to us.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.760
Um, where's the president?

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.680
Right in front of you.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.760
See?

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.220
In front of me?

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.620
After-School Pleiades

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.790
Sobbingly, I went on my journey

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:09.250
Wishing I could at least fly through the sky

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.630
And yet the stars gently shone on me in the nights after our quarrels

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:21.180
I wonder if you were also watching them

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.440
I don't know... I want to know... I want to feel it...

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:33.480
Nothingness simply means there are infinite possibilities

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.280
The excitement I got after realizing that

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.370
was like surfing the waves of space and time

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:45.460
How strange that I'm not afraid anymore

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:48.170
Let's embrace our imperfections and go on

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:51.040
We'll open the promised door

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.220
and gain dazzling smiles!

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:17.990
The Final Light and His Name

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.490
days until Shimotsuki Festival!!

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.790
You can't transform, either?

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:24.540
No.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.000
And your drive shaft?

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:31.830
I guess it was too optimistic to
hope it'd fix itself overnight.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:35.510
But why has only Subaru lost her magic?

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.170
Somewhere in your heart,

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:45.060
you're actually wishing that collecting the
fragments would never end, aren't you?

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.350
<i>Subaru...</i>

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.730
You'll be back to normal
once you get some more rest.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.320
No, that's most likely impossible.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.990
Only those with undetermined potentials,

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.320
those who are still nothing, can use magic.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.570
If Subaru's lost her ability to use magic,

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:07.330
it might be because she's "become something."

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:11.580
Once you've chosen a path, you can't go back,

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.840
and the potentials you lost will never return.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.210
How can you say such an ominous thing?!

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.800
Then what about gathering the fragments?

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.090
What will happen to that?

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.720
The five of us have always done
that together, so without Subaru...

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.100
The culture festival is starting.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:30.060
We can't have the culture festival like this.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.860
Cosplay Research Club,

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.480
fight on!

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.700
Cosplay Research Club, fight on!

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.450
Aoi?

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.200
Let's hold the culture festival!

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:46.450
But...

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.870
This year's culture festival only happens once.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.460
There won't be a second time.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.750
You're right...

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:55.080
No, wait, it might be the first
time for you, but for us...

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.960
We've already prepared for it so I want to
hold the culture festival with everyone!

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.850
Welcome to Shimotsuki Festival!!

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.310
Well...

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.560
We can't do anything until
we get a new meteor forecast,

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.440
so we'd be missing out if we didn't enjoy it.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.320
Subaru, we'll take turns helping out,

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.820
so let's see the planetarium through, too.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.700
Itsuki, Hikaru...

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.120
If you don't do it, Subaru, who will?

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.910
All right, it's settled!

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.120
Okay, all together!

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.880
Cosplay Research Club!

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.500
Fight on!

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:52.980
Preparing

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:53.480
House of

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:53.480
Fortunes

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.400
One more, okay?

00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.400
Okay!

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.530
It looks very good on you.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:07.870
Can you find the three stars
lined up next to each other

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.160
Planetarium

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.160
in progress

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.120
like friends in the winter night sky?

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.830
With those three at its center,

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.790
the first-magnitude star above
and to the left is Betelgeuse,

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.580
the one below and to the right is Rigel,

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:22.510
and together, the hourglass-shaped
constellation they form is known as Orion.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:27.010
If you look directly left from Orion's Betelgeuse,

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.510
you find Canis Minor's
first-magnitude star, Procyon.

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:33.890
Subaru!

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.480
D-Dad, what's wrong?

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.650
I tried to record your brave performance...

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:42.780
But it was so dark, nothing showed up!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.990
And you worked so hard...

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.660
Come on, calm down.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.370
Did you understand everything about the stars?

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.910
Of course! I understood it very clearly!

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:57.460
It made me realize how much you've
changed before I even knew it.

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.170
What's wrong, Subaru?

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.970
Did I say something I shouldn't have?

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.010
<i>You're wrong...</i>

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:16.520
<i>I haven't changed at all.</i>

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:23.400
This concludes the 36th Shimotsuki Festival.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:27.240
Due to the rain, the after-festival
will be held in the gym.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.950
Aww!

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.910
Thank you all for your hard work.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.290
So it's finally here...

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.210
The last meteor forecast.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.170
Isn't it about time for the meteor forecast?

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:51.050
Sorry I'm late. Do we have a meteor forecast?

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:53.300
Oh, good. You're all still here!

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:57.730
Why were you making preparations by yourself?

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.850
For the final fragment,

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:04.190
I felt that I should go alone.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:07.940
Why would you say that now,
after getting us so deeply involved?

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.030
I don't know how far I'll have to go...

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.080
And I can't involve you all any further.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:18.700
Then if we go because we want to,
there's no problem, right?

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.500
We had lots of fun at the culture festival,

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.040
so now we can go after the
fragment without regrets.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.460
We all came to this decision ourselves.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.130
We're all ready.

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:29.760
You guys...

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:56.160
<i>There's no more strawberry milk.</i>

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.650
There's a meteor forecast.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:29.440
I see.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:32.820
I've decided to go.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.110
Okay.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:35.610
Everyone else, too.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.240
Okay.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.040
I hope the rain stops.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:47.590
He said the final fragment is very far away,

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:51.920
but I'm sure we'll be able to
get it and come back home.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.430
Yeah. I believe in you.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.180
I believe in you, too.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:56.890
Huh?

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.140
No matter what the president says...

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.140
You can change, Subaru!

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.440
Aoi...

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:30.960
<i>It's full of weeds.</i>

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:34.220
<i>And we were tending it until just recently...</i>

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.970
<i>It's as if none of it ever happened.</i>

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.720
Hey, bedhead. You're alone today?

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:41.350
Huh?

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:42.850
Hey.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:47.480
I mean, you always came here with him, right?

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:49.520
Him?

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.230
You know, the guy from our class.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.240
The one who always seemed spaced out.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:55.610
Uh...

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:57.910
Huh? That's weird.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.870
I can't recall his name.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:03.870
Ah, hey...

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.250
What are you doing?

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:18.840
It's here!

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:19.590
What's wrong?

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.730
Um... Thank you very much!

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.560
S-Sure...

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:38.320
The final fragment is moving farther
away from us at immense speed.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.740
Then let's get going!

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.950
Now, hold on.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:44.330
What is it now?

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.250
Just chasing after it blindly won't work.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.660
Then what do we do?

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:51.380
Thanks to the fragments we've collected,
our meteor forecast can now tell us

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:55.050
both the fragment's momentum and
its coordinates at the same time!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.050
So we can tell where the fragment is?

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:00.890
And this time, we'll be
making use of dark energy.

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.340
Dark energy?

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:03.510
Sounds scary.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.180
The Energy of Darkness...

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:07.770
Is it safe to use such an evil-sounding power?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:11.690
Humanity only recently identified it.
There's no other name for it!

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:15.440
Dark energy comprises over 60% of
the energy in the entire universe.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.570
It's the most common energy out there!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:19.190
Wow...

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:23.490
Using this energy, the driving force
behind the universe's expansion,

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.910
we should be able to catch up to the fragment,
no matter how quickly it's moving.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.210
Same old bogus stuff...

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.080
How rude! This is science!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.750
It's not magic?

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.880
I don't quite understand, but all right.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.460
Now then, let's start!

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:42.470
Oh, it's the Moon!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.720
That brings back memories!

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.560
Now, let's go!

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.190
Apate...

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.940
Huh? Didn't it light up last time?

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:00.110
That's still in the future.

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:02.700
That's right. Nanako hasn't reached it yet!

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.870
Is this some time paradox?!

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:05.990
On to the next one!

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:11.160
Now we're outside our solar system.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:13.540
The Sun is that small?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:17.500
We really are traveling faster than
the speed of light, aren't we?

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:18.420
Yeah...

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.100
It looks like there are fewer planets.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:28.810
Behind you is our galaxy.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.520
We left the galaxy?!

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.140
We're headed the right way, right?

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:35.940
Yes, we should be.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:40.320
It's pitch black.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.110
Is this really space?

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.200
I can't see any stars.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.950
Those weren't stars. They were all galaxies.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:50.910
We've traveled about two
hundred thousand light years.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:53.830
There's nothing else here but us.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:56.130
How many more times do we need to jump?

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.590
Something isn't right.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:02.130
We're not getting any closer to the fragment.
It's only getting farther away.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.090
What does that mean?

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:06.220
But we're already going faster
than the speed of light...

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:11.970
Space itself is expanding at a rate faster
than the speed of light, so it's not unfeasible.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:13.810
You saw the space chart, right?

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:14.730
Space chart?

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.230
The one hung up in the science lab?

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:17.980
We have one of those?

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:18.690
We do.

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:21.480
Anyway, no matter how much we accelerate,

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.990
if the fragment is accelerating even faster,

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:27.240
then there's no guarantee we'll catch up to it.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:28.870
Let's turn back.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:34.500
Even I can't imagine what might happen
to us if we continue this pursuit.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.250
But without the fragments, your spaceship...

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.710
We collected twelve fragments.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:43.130
That's enough to keep the spaceship
from materializing for a while.

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:44.590
How long is a while?

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:47.510
At the least, I guarantee it'll
last longer than your lifetimes.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:49.430
But if it materializes...

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:52.010
Then it will perish and take Earth with it.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:53.390
We can't let that happen!

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:58.400
But if we can't capture the fragment,
even with all of you here,

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.900
then the only possible reason

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:04.490
is that this universe is forbidding
the fragments from being collected.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:06.700
You mean it's pointless to even try?

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:08.820
Now that you possess the power of magic,

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:13.660
this universe is currently operating
slightly in your favor.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:18.460
All your wishes up to now, big or small,
have come true, haven't they?

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:22.380
Are you saying that's all thanks to magic?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:26.050
If we can't gather the
fragments in this universe...

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:31.300
That means you yourselves
don't desire it to happen.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:36.640
One could also say it's as if you all
are wishing, deep in your hearts,

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:37.890
to remain in this universe.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:38.810
But that's...

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:40.560
Even if that is the case,

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:47.070
it only means it was my mistake to make
you all magic users in light of your potential.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.950
Now, let's return to Earth.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:52.740
I'll go.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.740
I made my decision when I left Earth.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:58.710
I decided to get the fragment and go back home.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.830
Because Subaru believes in me,
and she's waiting for me!

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.670
I'll go, too. I already made up my mind.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:08.670
We didn't do this because of the universe.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:12.640
We did this all of our own will
and our own strength.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:16.560
Besides, if we give up now,
we can't ever change.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.270
Everyone, think about this.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.020
If you continue pursuing the fragment,

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:22.100
you might end up outside this universe's law—

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.190
Shut up.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:24.770
Nice, Nanako!

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.320
Uh, what's this switch?

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:28.280
That's...

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.360
That's...

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:33.200
Yeah, there's no mistake.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.910
I can see the fragment's light.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:40.160
You mean... You can see the fragment?

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:42.670
Can I place my hopes in you?

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:43.920
President.

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:49.840
It's true that we all wished to
stay magic users forever.

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:54.340
But we all became magic users
because we wanted to change.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:56.600
We can't end it like this.

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.780
<i>It's no use.</i>

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:12.800
I don't know anything about Minato...

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.680
Oh, right!

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:25.560
Yesterday, I made a star, too.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:26.600
A star?

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:29.520
Yeah! I made it with my mom,
using folding paper.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:30.650
I'll give it to you.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:32.230
Oh...

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:33.690
What's wrong?

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.330
I thought you could put it up as a decoration,

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:43.080
but you wouldn't be able to see it at all...

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.580
I like this star.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:50.340
Really?

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:54.130
Really. Because this star is like me.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:55.050
Huh?

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.980
I'll give you this star of mine in return.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.350
Are you sure?

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.770
I can just gather more.

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:14.230
Besides, it looks like this star likes you, too.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.740
Wow, it's so pretty!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:28.670
<i>I thought I had cherished that
mysterious star he gave me...</i>

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:38.220
Have you really disappeared, Minato?

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.390
Minato...

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:45.740
See?

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:50.000
Neither you nor I are illusions.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:52.870
Huh?

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:58.880
This is...

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:20.030
Minato...

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.400
What you see now is the true me.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.360
I didn't avoid choosing.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:27.780
I had already lost the potential
to choose from the beginning.

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:32.540
That's why you're gathering the fragments.

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.120
That's right.

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:36.790
And then, I'll disappear from this world.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:41.300
Then I'll open your door
as many times as it takes!

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:53.600
How many was that?

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:54.900
I don't know anymore.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:57.940
Forget it, just jump, jump, jump!

00:20:57.940 --> 00:20:59.150
Hey, Subaru.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:20:59.860
Huh?

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:03.990
Was that the others?

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:07.910
Subaru, you should go where you belong.

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:10.490
I am me, and you are you!

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:11.700
Minato!

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:18.000
See? It really was Subaru!

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.300
S-Subaru?! Why are you here?

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.800
That outfit... Your magic's back!

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:24.420
That's great, Subarun!

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:27.050
This is a completely new magic!

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:30.060
Where are we right now?

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:32.060
I don't know any of these constellations.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.940
We're partway through our seventh galaxy.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.060
Seventh?!

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:39.060
We're having trouble capturing the last fragment.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:40.070
Oh...

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.780
I want to change.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.200
It's not too late yet, is it?

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:47.700
Of course it's not!

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:49.120
We've been waiting for you.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.450
We can't do it without you, Subaru.

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:57.080
I'll never give up!

00:21:57.210 --> 00:22:00.090
To Be Continued

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:11.720
You see, when I looked up

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:17.100
everyone was smiling at me

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:26.820
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:35.790
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:22:30.370 --> 00:22:33.160
...my daily life...

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:45.550
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:47.420
"Can I fly?"

00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:51.640
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:57.270
We can go there whenever we want to

00:22:57.270 --> 00:23:06.940
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:11.570
"We have to catch them!"

00:23:11.570 --> 00:23:16.080
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:21.420
the scenery around us glittered

00:23:21.670 --> 00:23:26.130
sometime after school

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:33.680
How did you manage to obtain that outfit, Subaru?

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:35.970
You already know, don't you?

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:37.180
We just saw him.

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:38.730
It's thanks to him, right?

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:41.690
Final Episode:
At the Water's Edge.

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:43.980
I just can't accept this after all!
